# TRANSPORTATION COST MATRIX
Transportation cost matrix submitted by the distribution teams from each warehouse is used to calculate the transportation cost of each bar. It includes the average vehicle condition ( in terms of fuel efficiency), road condition which could significantly affect transportation cost due to wear and tear maintenance cost, actual amount of fuel in each of the locations( note that it varies slightly) and fuel availability which is another important constraint to be considered in Nigeria transportation system.

# Cost of transporting each bar
Using the magnitudes of feasible distances from the warehouses to the markets, the cost of transporting each bar is calculated (Table image attached with document), taking into consideration the variables in the submitted matrix including road condition (RC) and fuel availability (FA) factor.

# Solution Models
The Linear Programming model was programmed into a Linear Programming Software (LiPS 1.11.1). Variables ranging from X1 to X12.  Each Variable represent possible values that need to be shipped from specific warehouse to specific seasonal market to achieve optimum cost of distribution.
X1 – Ikere to Lagos
X2 – Ikere to Ibadan
X3 – Ikere to Sagamu
X4 – Ikere to Okitipupa
X4 – Benin to Lagos
X6 – Benin to Ibadan
X7 – Benin to Okitipupa
X8 – Benin to Sagamu
X9 – Offa to Lagos
X10 – Offa to Ibadan
X11 – Offa to Sagamu
X12 – Offa to Okitipupa
The Objective Function is to minimize cost as much as possible whilst fulfilling the market demand. 
Computed using function “min” while summing the product of the possible quantities from each warehouse and respective cost of shipping per unit bar of steel.

The model Labelled “A” represent the DEMAND constraints summing up to the forecasted demand (17,000 in Lagos, 14,500 in Ibadan, 11,000 in Sagamu and 8300 in Okitipupa)
The model labelled “B” represent the SUPPLY constraints which may be less than or equal to the capacity of each respective warehouse (20,000 in Ikere, 22,000 in Benin City and 20,000 in Offa)

